        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(signal): add timeouts to container REST requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSignal container REST requests already had a timeout around the fetch call, but the timer was cleared as soon as response headers arrived. A slow or hanging response body could still block REST send/status and attachment paths indefinitely.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nKeep the existing timeout active until callers finish reading or releasing the response body. The change preserves the existing fetch helper, bounded body readers, cleanup path, and caller upload/attachment semantics.\n\n## User Impact\n\nIf the signal-cli REST container returns headers and then stalls, OpenClaw now aborts the request during body reading instead of leaving Signal operations pending forever.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/client-container.test.ts` passed: 62 tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/signal/src/client-container.ts extensions/signal/src/client-container.test.ts` passed.\n- Remote Testbox/Crabbox validation was attempted, but the local wrapper rejected the selected crabbox binary during sanity checks, so focused local wrapper tests were used instead.\n",
